      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T13:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t we use a `SpinMutex` or an atomic and keep those functions safe? I\u0027m not sure why `ERRNO` is `pub`, does C link against the symbol directly?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac652603_e65ba597",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T13:31:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the problem is the `__errno()` function which needs to return a pointer to it.",
      "parentUuid": "7f054008_4bbea875",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82501c7e_c0b6d33e",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T16:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, does that prevent `set_errno()` and `get_errno()` from being safe by using mutex/atomic? As a result, you wouldn\u0027t need to propagate the \"`must only be called from the main thread`\" comment/requirement to all these other functions.",
      "parentUuid": "ac652603_e65ba597",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52d51575_4df7ffbe",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T18:06:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `ERRNO` were a `SpinMutex\u003cc_int\u003e` then how could `__errno` return a `*mut c_int`?",
      "parentUuid": "82501c7e_c0b6d33e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58339aed_a33a61e8",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T11:27:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t it be an `AtomicI32`, which provides the safe `.load()`/`.store()` but also `.as_ptr()` for `__errno()`?",
      "parentUuid": "52d51575_4df7ffbe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cea4530_e2ffac9f",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T11:37:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the caller of `__errno()` does non-atomic reads or writes with the pointer returned from an `AtomicI32` then there is still undefined behaviour. The only way around this is to remove `__errno()` entirely or change the contract for the caller, which I guess you can\u0027t do.",
      "parentUuid": "58339aed_a33a61e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "294d63fd_c6eebb6b",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T12:46:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, but then only `__errno()` is `unsafe`, right?",
      "parentUuid": "1cea4530_e2ffac9f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b136415a5d6ce3594900b60f0249f597eb53adc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7b83845_dded4f57",
        "filename": "libs/libvmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T13:30:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, but then the safety requirement of `__errno()` would be that its callers must only use atomic operations to access the contents of the pointer it returns. Can you change all the callers of `__errno()` to do that?",
      "parentUuid": "294d63fd_c6eebb6b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 20
      },
